## Key Design Moves

**1. Chromatic aberration on the main type** — Three overlapping layers with cyan offset left, magenta offset right, white on top. Screams "gritty" without extra software.

**2. Semi-transparent skewed blocks** — Using `mix-blend-mode: screen` and `overlay` lets your underexposed photo show through while adding color atmosphere. The skew makes it feel off-kilter and energetic.

**3. Built-in grain + scanlines** — The SVG turbulence filter and CSS repeating gradient add texture that'll unify any photo you drop in. If your photo is *extra* grainy, dial down `--noise-opacity` in the CSS variables.

**4. Knockout stroke type** — The "NEON DECAY TOUR" line uses `-webkit-text-stroke` with transparent fill. Works great on dark backgrounds.

---

## How to Drop In Your Photo

Replace the `.photo-layer` div with:

```html
<div class="photo-layer">
  <img src="your-concert-photo.jpg" alt="">
</div>
```

And add this CSS:

```css
.photo-layer img {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  object-fit: cover;
  filter: brightness(0.5) contrast(1.3) saturate(0.7);
}
```

The low brightness + high contrast will pull detail out of underexposed shots while the overlay elements do the heavy lifting.

